<!--
    A lazy accessor on a Swift image returns the value of its cache cell
    (`option cachereturn on|off`, default on, Swift images only).

    `void *get(void) { void *v = g; if (v) return v; v = make(); g = v; return v; }`
    leaves in x0, at the RETURN, the load of `g` on one path and the value
    stored into `g` on the other. upstream's ancestorOpUse refuses both (the
    load is branched on, the stored value is stored), so the function printed
    `void` and its callers read a result it does not have. Swift's lazy
    witness-table accessors and its mangled-name type cache are this shape.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 output-prototype. p4_calls/kuna_cachereturn.rs takes
    a return trial in an output register of the model when every value
    reaching each live RETURN is a load of one cell or a call's result stored
    into it, at least one of each, and the image's source language is Swift.

    Chunk 0x1000a8, clang 22 -O2 -fno-pic for aarch64-linux-gnu (make is in
    another translation unit):
      void *g_cache, *g_other;
      void *get_cached(void) { void *v = g_cache; if (v) return v; v = make(); g_cache = v; return v; }
      void ensure(void) { if (!g_other) g_other = make(); }
            (control: a void function tests the cell in x8; it stays void)
      void *get_slot(void **slot) { void *v = *slot; if (v) return v; v = make(); *slot = v; return v; }
            (the cell is behind a parameter)
    get_split at 0x10012c is hand-written in the shape of a Swift lazy
    witness-table accessor: `ldr x0,[g]; cbz x0,1f; ret; 1: ... bl make;
    adr x8,g; stlr x0,[x8]; ... ret` (two RETURNs, the store a release).

    The chunk has no language signal, so the first two passes force
    `option sourcelang swift`. Pass 1 (`option cachereturn off`) reproduces
    the bug: get_cached, get_slot and get_split print void. Pass 2 is the
    shipped default on a Swift image: they return the cell's value. Pass 3
    (`option sourcelang c`) is the shipped default on a C image: the rule is
    inert (gcc AArch64 compiles a void initializer to an accessor's bytes),
    so every function prints void. ensure stays void in every pass.
-->
